From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FramePlayer contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] gamepad: hapticActuators and pulse() for WebXR
 controllers

Many WebXR pages vibrate controllers with the Gamepad Extensions API that
Meta Quest's browser exposes:
inputSource.gamepad.hapticActuators[0].pulse(value, duration). Babylon.js,
many three.js games and Fire Fight 2's Rave Raid do this. Chromium has
neither, so `hapticActuators?.[0]?.pulse?.()` quietly does nothing and
those pages never vibrate. playEffect pages (0008) do vibrate.

- Gamepad.hapticActuators: a frozen array holding the gamepad's vibration
  actuator, if it has one. The array object stays the same while the
  actuator does.
- GamepadHapticActuator.pulse(value, duration): a dual-rumble effect at
  |value| for |duration| ms. It goes through the same delegate (XR
  controllers, 0008) or gamepad-service path as playEffect. Out-of-range
  values are clamped, as on Quest. It resolves true once the pulse has
  played, or once a newer effect has replaced it. It resolves false if
  the device can't play it.

Applies on top of 0008.
---
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/gamepad/gamepad.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/gamepad/gamepad.cc
index 809a66c521..08970d29a1 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/gamepad/gamepad.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/gamepad/gamepad.cc
@@ -208,6 +208,23 @@ GamepadHapticActuator* Gamepad::vibrationActuator() const {
   return client_->GetVibrationActuatorForGamepad(*this);
 }
 
+const FrozenArray<GamepadHapticActuator>& Gamepad::hapticActuators() {
+  // The same array while the vibration actuator stays the same.
+  GamepadHapticActuator* actuator = vibrationActuator();
+  if (!haptic_actuators_ ||
+      haptic_actuators_->size() != (actuator ? 1u : 0u) ||
+      (actuator && (*haptic_actuators_)[0] != actuator)) {
+    HeapVector<Member<GamepadHapticActuator>> actuators;
+    if (actuator) {
+      actuators.push_back(actuator);
+    }
+    haptic_actuators_ =
+        MakeGarbageCollected<FrozenArray<GamepadHapticActuator>>(
+            std::move(actuators));
+  }
+  return *haptic_actuators_.Get();
+}
+
 void Gamepad::SetVibrationActuatorInfo(
     const device::GamepadHapticActuator& actuator) {
   has_vibration_actuator_ = actuator.not_null;
@@ -238,6 +255,7 @@ void Gamepad::Trace(Visitor* visitor) const {
   visitor->Trace(client_);
   visitor->Trace(buttons_);
   visitor->Trace(touch_events_);
+  visitor->Trace(haptic_actuators_);
   ScriptWrappable::Trace(visitor);
 }
 
